(i) Appeal is partly allowed;
(ii) The impugned judgment and award is modified;
(iii) The petitioners are entitled to enhanced compensation of Rs.29,620/- with interest at the rate of 6% per annum from the date of petition till its realization;
(iv) Respondent Nos.1 and 3 are liable to pay compensation;
(v) The respondent No.2/Insurance Company being the insurer of the Andhra lorry is directed to deposit the entire compensation with interest @ 6% within eight weeks from the date of receipt of certified copy of this judgment, with liberty to work out its remedy to recover the same from the owner and insurer of the Maharashtra lorry either - 13 - NC: 2024:KHC:37842 in the same proceedings or in a separate proceedings;

opennyai_summary.decision:
In view of Section 149(1) of the Act,
notwithstanding that the insurer may be entitled to avoid its liability, he shall pay the compensation.
The actionable negligence is against the driver of Maharashtra lorry and for this reason, he was charge sheeted.
The Insurance Company has to satisfy the award and work out its remedy to recover - 12 - NC: 2024:KHC:37842 the compensation from the owner and insurer of the Maharashtra lorry.
